<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomon I of Imereti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1735">1735</a>–<a href="/years/1784">1784</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagrationi dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> I was king of Imereti in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1752 to 1784, with an interruption in the 1760s. He defeated an Ottoman army in 1757, curbed the power of his great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> and banned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> that had drained the kingdom's population. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erekle-ii">Erekle II</a> of Kartli-Kakheti, he fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1768-1774">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1768–1774, after which Ottoman control over Imereti weakened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomon-i-of-imereti.jpg" alt="Solomon I of Imereti" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Surprizi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solomon_I_of_Imereti_(National_museum_of_Georgia).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Two battles fought at Chikhori shaped Imereti’s history: Bagrat’s victory over George VIII in 1463 and <b>Solomon I</b>’s victory over the Ottomans in 1757.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-imereti">Kingdom of Imereti · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42.27,42.71&amp;year=1766" aria-label="Kutaisi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5586 660 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Solomon I of Imereti"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6036 930h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6036 930h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42.27,42.71&amp;year=1766">What was here in 1766? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
